WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.130
All right.

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:03.650
Let's get into audience questions for the
week.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.850
Very important, relevant questions that tie
together a lot of the different issues that

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:08.960
we've been discussing.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.769
First one is, hey, David, if the third quarter
numbers really are as good as Donald Trump

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:18.050
predicts, could that rocket trump to reelection
on November 3rd?

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.439
So understand the timing.

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:23.359
First quarter is a January, February, March.

00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:28.560
The first quarter numbers came out on April
30th as an estimate, and then they were more

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.410
fine tuned on May 30th, the second quarter,
April, May, June.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.930
We got estimated second quarter numbers on
July 30th.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:43.250
And then we will get presumably more accurate
and precise numbers on August 30th.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:50.830
So that means that for the third quarter,
July, August, September, we will get estimates

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:54.400
of GDP on October 30th.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.610
That is four days before the presidential
election.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:02.600
So I would not just be thinking it's possible.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:10.250
I would be thinking it's almost a guarantee
that on October 30th there will be good GDP

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.250
numbers.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.250
Why?

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.250
Why will they be good?

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:17.259
Well, one, the GDP goes down more than 30
percent.

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:24.490
You have a new significantly lower baseline,
a record low baseline, meaning any increase

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.310
is going to seem relatively larger now.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.979
Bear in mind, think about the number one.

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:34.439
If you start at one hundred and you lose 30
percent, you're down at 70.

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:39.659
If you then gain 20 percent, you go back up
to 84.

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:40.740
Down 30 percent.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.740
Up 20 percent.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.999
You started 100.

00:01:42.999 --> 00:01:44.500
You go down to 70.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.460
You go back up to 84.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.369
You will hear Trump claim on October 30th.

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:54.350
This is the biggest rise in GDP in American
history.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:59.889
And it will be true on a percentage basis
because of that new lower base of 70.

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:01.049
So to speak.

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:03.409
But we will still be at 84.

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:06.780
We will still be imagining it's 20 percent
up.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:12.220
We will still be down 16 percent from where
we were before the second quarter.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:18.260
So will the economy really be doing great
when we get that announcement?

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.390
No.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.000
Will Donald Trump try to take credit for it?

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Of course.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.900
And will Donald Trump claim that it is the
best GDP result we have ever had?

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:29.900
Yes.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.470
Now, I am worried about this.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.930
I genuinely am worried about it.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:34.930
Why?

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:39.310
Because there's a lot of really ignorant people.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:44.910
There is a lot of easily manipulable or manipulatable.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.470
I don't know if either or both are words people.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.850
And there are also people who really don't
want to vote for Joe Biden.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.220
And they will look for any excuse not to do
it.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:59.300
And so inevitably, we need to plan for it
on October 30th.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:05.540
We will have 96 hours before the election
during which we will need to fight the talking

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:12.250
point that no one has ever overseen a bigger
GDP increase in a single quarter than Donald

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:13.250
Trump.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.330
And it will be true.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:20.110
But, of course, it will not be reflective
of the broader economic situation.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:23.910
And that is really what we what we all need
to remember.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:28.280
And listen, this gets me back to polls, says
Biden's up nine.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.210
Margin of error is three point five.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:35.460
That means it's possible Biden's really only
winning by two.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:42.590
If Trump swings just one percent of the population
on October 30th by saying, look at this great

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:48.750
GDP victory, that might mean Biden wins the
popular vote by one.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:54.430
And you can, as we know from 2016, you can
win the popular vote and still lose the Electoral

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:55.430
College.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:56.470
We've seen that with Hillary Clinton.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.590
We saw it with Al Gore in the year 2000.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.300
We've actually seen it several times.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.210
So we need to be very, very vigilant.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.310
There's going to be we need to plan for it.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.310
Okay.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:09.710
And in fact, this is where Democrats are just
terrible.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:17.049
We know this is going to happen on October
30th. Trump will claim that he is fixed everything

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:19.530
and brought us the biggest economic plan a
little better.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.530
You all know.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.650
You know, economic prosperity, all that stuff.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:28.860
What do we do for those 96 hours to ensure
to ensure that it doesn't work to swing the

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.200
election in his favor?

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.850
I don't know what the answer is, but it's
going to happen.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.650
And we damn bell damn well better have a plan.

